# Keep the root manifest and lockfile visible to Nx inside the bug agent's
# sandbox (#1370). When Claude Code starts with its subprocess env scrub on, it
# appends /package.json and /package-lock.json, among others, to
# .git/info/exclude. Nx's file walker honours that file, so without these
# lines the lockfile plugin never sees package-lock.json, the project graph
# holds no npm packages, and every target that names an external dependency
# fails ("The externalDependency 'jest' ... could not be found").
#
# This works together with cli.packageManager in nx.json: the same startup
# leaves an empty yarn.lock on disk, which Nx would otherwise pick over
# package-lock.json. Either one alone still leaves the graph without npm
# packages. Outside the sandbox nothing excludes these files, so the lines
# change nothing.
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
